x0g|v|To be at the head of; to put one's self at the head of; to lead; to direct; to act as leader to; as, to head an army, an expedition, or a riot. ; To form a head to; to fit or furnish with a head; as, to head a nail. ; To behead; to decapitate. ; To cut off the top of; to lop off; as, to head trees. ; To go in front of; to get in the front of, so as to hinder or stop; to oppose; hence, to check or restrain; as, to head a drove of cattle; to head a person; the wind heads a ship. ; To set on the head; as, to head a cask. ; To originate; to spring; to have its source, as a river. ; To go or point in a certain direction; to tend; as, how does the ship head? ; To form a head; as, this kind of cabbage heads early.	s:giq,65,2;1bo0,46,2;1t6r,43,1;1wm9,17,2;1uf8,16,1;24m4,15,4;1lxc,11,1;1jyd,9,2;22aw,9,1;mpp,7,1;1g17,7,1;vu4,4,4~vu4,4,4;24m4,15,4;giq,65,2;1bo0,46,2;1jyd,9,2;1wm9,17,2;1t6r,43,1;1uf8,16,1;1g17,7,1;mpp,7,1;1lxc,11,1;22aw,9,1	D:1wav,5,2~1wav,5,2
